[17592186263509 1145 "We can find the acceleration of an object by computing the slope of its speed-time graph. So, let's draw an example of a speed-time graph where the speed is measured in $\\text{in/min}$ and the time is measured in $\\text{min}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945962/assets/ecdd2f132499a6be0c1d8fa48f021713e2019ed9e6660af041853f7e30766091.png)\n\nIn this case, the slope is computed as\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{\\text{change in speed}}{\\text{change in time}},\n$$\n\nand so the units of the slope are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{units of speed}}{\\text{units of time}}=\\frac{\\text{in/min}}{\\text{min}}=\\frac{\\text{in}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\text{min}}=\\frac{\\text{in}}{{\\text{min}}^{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the units of acceleration are $\\frac{\\text{in}}{{\\text{min}}^{2}}.$" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263511 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263512 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263513 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263514 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263515 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1041 "selection" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263514 13194139533888 true] [17592186263510 1110 #uuid "3db0d838-d4f7-5a89-a440-cc45c8e6877f" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263511 1034 "\\frac{\\text{in}}{{\\text{min}}^{3}}" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263511 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533888 true] [17592186263511 1111 #uuid "4fa2eeb6-b039-5229-854e-7efb3f96e96b" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263512 1034 "\\frac{{\\text{in}}^{2}}{{\\text{min}}^{2}}" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263512 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533888 true] [17592186263512 1111 #uuid "941d6c78-75be-57f3-ae76-1b5798921f2c" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263513 1034 "\\frac{{\\te