sents the motion of a $250\\text{cc}$ motorcycle at the start of a race. Calculate the acceleration of the motorcycle." 13194139533888 true] [17592186263537 1113 #uuid "b4ac1e14-f74c-5d5c-a627-57b051b36814" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263537 1145 "In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line.\n\nThe line passes through the points $(0,0)$ and $(8,28),$ so its slope is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{28\\,\\text{m/s}-0\\,\\text{m/s}}{8\\,\\text{s}-0\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{28\\,\\text{m/s}}{8\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =3.5\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration of the $250\\text{cc}$ motorcycle is $3.5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263539 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263540 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263541 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263542 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263543 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1041 "selection" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263539 13194139533888 true] [17592186263538 1110 #uuid "33d00f6a-f71e-54ef-9fe2-2388eaea42aa" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263539 1034 "3.5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263539 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533888 true] [17592186263539 1111 #uuid "24d1d84b-aa4d-500b-9211-76f7a789085e" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263540 1034 "2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263540 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533888 true] [17592186263540 1111 #uuid "61cb8e6b-4381-5212-94ab-2b10ea57c883" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263541 1034 "5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263541 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533888 true] [17592186263541 1111 #uuid "44fa14bc-b4e8-538e-8cb7-95a872020aa2" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263542 1034 "2.5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533888 true] [17592186263542 1111 #uuid "db02e0dc-c22d-55da-b978-803853877155" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263543 1034 "4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263543 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533888 true] [17592186263543 1111 #uuid "bdd44afb-5e52-58cd-b17f-924c0a6ca9e5" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263544 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263545 13194139533888 true] [17592186263544 1089 "q-108462" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263544 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533888 true] [17592186263544 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945962/assets/31e0e843eb581f01cdc7ebb5273398a3c0f32d2949b9e36cd28423295d7b76e8.png)\n\nThe speed-time graph shown above represents the motion of a $250\\text{cc}$ motorcycle. At what times is the motorcycle accelerating?" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263544 1113 #uuid "c47c1778-9762-5608-84e1-7206031f9c36" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263544 1145 "The motorcycle is accelerating when its acceleration is positive. In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line. So, we need to find the times for which the slope is positive.\n\nWe see from the graph that the slope is positive from $t=30\\,\\text{s}$ to $t=60\\,\\text{s}.$ Therefore, the $250\\text{cc}$ motorcycle is accelerating in this time interval." 13194139533888 true] [17592186263545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263546 13194139533888 true] [17592186263545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263547 13194139533888 true] [17592186263545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263548 13194139533888 true] [17592186263545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263549 13194139533888 true] [17592186263545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263550 13194139533888 true] [17592186263545 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533888 true] [17592186263545 1041 "selection" 13194139533888 true] [17592186263545 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263547 13194139533888 true] [1